.TH AEGISROUTE 1 "October 2026" "AegisRoute 3.0.0" "Advaitik Intelligence"
.SH NAME
aegisroute \- multi-protocol Linux traceroute intelligence and route analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aegisroute
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AegisRoute
resolves a target and runs the native Linux
.BR traceroute (8)
backend with UDP, TCP, ICMP, or all three probe strategies. Each strategy sends
probes with successively increasing TTL (IPv4) or hop-limit (IPv6) values.
Routers that expire the probes normally return ICMP time-exceeded responses.
AegisRoute parses those responses into hops, calculates loss and latency statistics,
optionally enriches public addresses, correlates paths, and produces findings.
.PP
When standard input is a terminal and no target is supplied, AegisRoute opens a
guided menu. Automation should provide a target and an explicit output format.
.PP
On Windows, AegisRoute automatically uses tracert.exe as an ICMP compatibility
backend. Every protocol selection returns a real ICMP route with a visible notice
that records the requested mode and actual backend. TCP/UDP packet semantics, flow
pinning, interface binding, IPv4 source binding, custom sample counts, and MTU
discovery require the full Linux backend; selecting them never causes a crash.
.SH MEASUREMENT DEFINITIONS
.TP
.B TTL / hop limit
The maximum number of routers a probe may cross. It increases from
.B --first-hop
through
.BR --max-hops .
.TP
.B RTT
Round-trip time from this system to a router or destination reply. It is not the
one-way delay of the individual link represented by the hop.
.TP
.B Loss
The percentage of probes at a TTL with no diagnostic reply. Intermediate routers
often rate-limit ICMP, so intermediate loss alone does not prove forwarded traffic loss.
.TP
.B Jitter
Population standard deviation of the observed RTT samples at a hop.
.TP
.B ECMP / multipath
More than one responder at one TTL, commonly caused by equal-cost load balancing.
.TP
.B ASN
Autonomous System Number identifying a network participating in Internet routing.
.SH PROBE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --backend " auto|native|scamper"
Select the measurement implementation. Auto uses native traceroute for classic
measurement and Scamper for Paris/MDA. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR --strategy " classic|paris|mda"
Select classic native traceroute, Scamper Paris flow-stable traceroute, or genuine
Scamper tracelb MDA. Paris and MDA require Scamper. Default: classic.
.TP
.BR --mda-confidence " 95|99"
MDA completeness confidence. A value of 99 sends more probes. Default: 95.
.TP
.BI --mda-max-probes " N"
Hard safety cap for one MDA measurement, from 100 through 10000. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI --scamper-binary " PATH"
Scamper executable. AEGISROUTE_SCAMPER changes the default.
.TP
.BR \-P , " --protocol " "udp|tcp|icmp|all"
Select UDP with a fixed destination port, TCP to the selected service port, ICMP
echo, or all three concurrently. The default is all. Cross-protocol differences
are reported as path divergence.
.TP
.BR \-p , " --port " PORT
Destination service port for TCP and UDP. Ignored by ICMP. Default: 443.
.TP
.BR \-q , " --probes " N
Samples per TTL, from 1 through 10. More samples improve statistics but increase
traffic and run time. Default: 3.
.TP
.BR \-m , " --max-hops " N
Highest TTL to probe, from 1 through 255. Default: 30.
.TP
.BR \-f , " --first-hop " N
First TTL to probe. Use a value above one only to skip known local hops. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-w , " --wait " SECONDS
Maximum wait for each reply before recording a timeout, from 0.05 through 60.
Default: 1.0 second.
.TP
.B \-4
Resolve and probe only IPv4. This is the default address family.
.TP
.B \-6
Resolve and probe only IPv6.
.TP
.BR \-i , " --interface " NAME
Bind probes to a Linux interface such as eth0, ens3, or wg0.
.TP
.BR \-s , " --source " ADDRESS
Bind probes to a configured local source IPv4 or IPv6 address.
.TP
.B --flow-consistent
Pin ports when the backend supports --sport. This Paris-inspired behavior reduces
false route changes caused by ECMP hashing; it is not full Paris Traceroute.
.TP
.BI --source-port " PORT"
Source port used with flow-consistent probing. Default: 33434.
.TP
.B --mtu
Request Linux traceroute path-MTU discovery when the backend supports --mtu.
.SH ENRICHMENT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --enrich " MODULES"
Comma-separated modules. rdns performs PTR DNS. asn uses Team Cymru. geo uses
ipwho.is. rpki requests RIPEstat validation and routing visibility. ixp checks
PeeringDB IXP LAN prefixes. Default: rdns,asn.
.TP
.B --no-enrich
Disable every external lookup. Private, loopback, link-local, carrier-NAT,
multicast, reserved, and unspecified addresses are still classified locally.
.TP
.BI --concurrency " N"
Maximum simultaneous DNS/geolocation lookups, from 1 through 128. ASN remains one
bulk request. Default: 16.
.SH ANALYSIS AND OUTPUT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --spike-threshold " MS"
Report a latency jump when average RTT rises by at least this amount from the
previous responding hop. Default: 35 milliseconds.
.TP
.BR --format " table|json|jsonl|csv|prometheus|html"
Choose the styled terminal dashboard, a JSON document, one compact JSON document
per line, flat CSV, Prometheus exposition, or standalone HTML. HTML requires
--output. Watch mode converts JSON to JSONL. Default: table.
.TP
.BR \-o , " --output " FILE
Write the report to FILE. Single reports use atomic replacement. Later watch
cycles append.
.TP
.BI --compare " REPORT.json"
Compare each protocol with an earlier AegisRoute JSON report and flag TTLs whose
responder sets changed.
.TP
.BI --watch " SECONDS"
Repeat the complete measurement after this interval (minimum one second) and
compare each cycle with the previous cycle.
.TP
.BI --cycles " N"
Stop watch mode after N cycles. Zero continues until Ctrl+C. Default: 0.
.TP
.BI --store " DATABASE"
Store reports, route fingerprints, and findings in a WAL-mode SQLite database.
.TP
.BI --history " N"
Print the latest N stored measurements for the target and exit. Requires --store.
.TP
.BI --atlas-id " ID"
Fetch and normalize an existing public RIPE Atlas traceroute measurement. This is
read-only and does not create a measurement or consume Atlas credits.
.TP
.BI --atlas-ids " ID,ID"
Fetch, normalize, and fuse several existing RIPE Atlas measurements.
.TP
.BI --merge-report " FILE"
Import a saved AegisRoute JSON report as another vantage. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --remote-report " HTTPS_URL"
Fetch a AegisRoute report from a read-only remote agent. Repeatable; HTTPS required.
.TP
.BI --remote-token " TOKEN"
Bearer token for remote agents. AEGISROUTE_REMOTE_TOKEN is preferred.
.TP
.B --bgp-events
Correlate observed prefixes with RIPEstat BGP announcements and withdrawals.
.TP
.BI --bgp-window " HOURS"
BGP lookback from 1 through 168 hours. Default: 24.
.TP
.BI --bgp-provider " ripestat|bgpstream"
Control-plane source. BGPStream requires the optional pybgpstream package.
Default: ripestat.
.TP
.B --service-check
Measure TCP connection reachability and timing on --port.
.TP
.B --tls-check
Perform a verified TLS handshake and report protocol, cipher, certificate, and time.
.TP
.B --alias-resolve
Actively test bounded alias candidates with Scamper Ally. Candidate selection is
not treated as confirmation.
.TP
.BI --alias-max-pairs " N"
Maximum Ally pairs, from 1 through 20. Default: 5.
.TP
.BI --tnt-output " FILE"
Import an external TNT text capture for hidden-MPLS correlation.
.TP
.BI --history-latency-delta " MS"
Historical RTT increase that creates a degradation finding. Default: 25.
.TP
.BI --webhook " HTTPS_URL"
POST threshold-matched findings as JSON. The payload is also Slack-compatible.
.TP
.BI --alert-severity " info|notice|warning|critical"
Minimum alert severity. Default: warning.
.TP
.BI --alert-mode " changes|all"
Send actionable route/security changes only, or all threshold-matched findings.
Default: changes.
.TP
.BI --email-to " ADDRESS"
Send threshold-matched findings by STARTTLS SMTP.
.TP
.BI --email-from " ADDRESS"
Sender required with --email-to.
.TP
.BI --smtp-host " HOST"
STARTTLS SMTP server required with --email-to.
.TP
.BI --smtp-port " PORT"
SMTP port. Default: 587.
.TP
.BI --smtp-user " USER"
Optional SMTP username. The password is read from AEGISROUTE_SMTP_PASSWORD.
.TP
.B --tui
Clear and redraw table output as a live console. Tab rotates protocol views, r
requests an immediate refresh, and q exits. Requires a terminal and table format.
.SH INTERFACE AND TROUBLESHOOTING OPTIONS
.TP
.B --interactive
Force the guided target, protocol, port, enrichment, format, and flow menu.
.TP
.B --demo
Run deterministic sample routes through parsing, analysis, and rendering. It sends
no DNS query, enrichment request, or probe packet.
.TP
.B --doctor
Print platform, Python, traceroute path, backend features, and Linux privilege
diagnostics, then exit.
.TP
.BI --binary " PATH"
Use another traceroute executable. AEGISROUTE_TRACEROUTE changes the default.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve the target and display exact traceroute commands without launching them.
.TP
.BI --company " NAME"
Set the company name in banners/reports. AEGISROUTE_COMPANY changes the default.
Built-in default: Advaitik Intelligence.
.TP
.BR --theme " amber|cyber|mono|ocean"
Choose the ANSI terminal palette. AEGISROUTE_THEME changes the default. Default: cyber.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI colors for logs, basic terminals, and assistive tools.
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Show detailed command help, definitions, privacy notes, and examples.
.TP
.B --version
Show the AegisRoute version.
.SH FINDINGS
AegisRoute can report silent hops, multiple responders, possible address loops,
ICMP unreachable annotations, latency jumps, incomplete paths, cross-protocol path
divergence, and baseline changes. These are diagnostic clues, not vulnerability claims.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one trace completed, or a demo/healthy doctor run succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid configuration, dependency/resolution failure, unhealthy doctor result, or
all requested probe engines failed.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.SH PRIVILEGES
UDP commonly works unprivileged. TCP or ICMP can require root/capabilities depending
on the distribution. Prefer narrow privileges on the packaged traceroute binary.
Never add setuid or capabilities to the Python script.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B aegisroute
Open the guided menu.
.TP
.B aegisroute --demo
Preview the interface without sending packets.
.TP
.B aegisroute example.com
Run all protocols with reverse-DNS and ASN enrichment.
.TP
.B aegisroute 1.1.1.1 -P tcp -p 443 --flow-consistent
Measure a flow-consistent HTTPS path.
.TP
.B aegisroute example.com --no-enrich --format json -o trace.json
Create JSON without external hop lookups.
.TP
.B aegisroute example.com --watch 30 --cycles 10 --format jsonl -o history.jsonl
Collect ten route snapshots at thirty-second intervals.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_COMPANY
Default company name.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_THEME
Default color theme.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_TRACEROUTE
Default traceroute executable.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_SCAMPER
Default Scamper executable.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_REMOTE_TOKEN
Bearer token used to fetch remote agent reports.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_AGENT_TOKEN
Bearer token required by aegisroute-agent.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_SMTP_PASSWORD
SMTP password; never place it directly in the command line.
.TP
.B AEGISROUTE_PYTHON
Python executable used by the Bash launcher.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/aegisroute
Default application directory.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/aegisroute
Default launcher symlink.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/aegisroute-agent
Read-only distributed report agent.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/aegisroute.1
Default manual page.
.SH SECURITY
AegisRoute is a single-target diagnostic tool, not a scanner. Use it only on networks
and systems you are authorized to measure. User values are passed as subprocess
argument arrays rather than shell commands.
